# GPU queue split (DTU LSF)

## Never use `bmod`

Students cannot change queue/walltime on existing jobs. To rebalance **PEND** jobs: **`bkill` + `bsub`** (user confirms). See [hpc-no-bmod.mdc](hpc-no-bmod.mdc).

Parse job IDs for `bkill` with: `bjobs -u $USER -p -noheader | awk '$1 ~ /^[0-9]+$/'` — raw `bjobs` output includes non-ID lines.

---

## Canonical queue mix (user preference)

**Per 10 jobs:** 5× `gpuv100`, 2× `gpua100`, 1× `gpua10`, 1× `gpul40s`, 1× `gpua40`.

Implementation: [`hpc/submit/cv4fold/_queue_mix.sh`](/work3/s204070/SPA/hpc/submit/cv4fold/_queue_mix.sh)

```bash
_pick_queue          # increments global JOB_IDX, sets PICKED_QUEUE
queue="${PICKED_QUEUE}"
```

**Never** use `queue="$(_pick_queue)"` — command substitution runs in a subshell and **JOB_IDX never increments** (all jobs land on v100).

Batch resubmit (kill PEND + mixed queues): `bash hpc/submit/cv4fold/submit_redistribute_pending_queues.sh`

---

## Walltimes (scheduling)

Request **~2× observed runtime** so LSF backfills faster (not 6h when ~1h suffices).

| Model | Wall | Basis |
|-------|------|--------|
| cHMM-GMVAE (3 seeds, 200 ep, joint) | **2:00** | ~60 min observed × 2 |
| cGMVAE (3 seeds, joint) | **1:30** | ~45 min est × 2 |

Within-lab runs are often faster but same walls are fine.

